IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa7-ch7`

-- coa7-ch3b.l4: Part 13 Chapter 3, Resolutions at meetings: notice of meetings (ss 307 to 313), lines 3942-4058 of
-- ukpga-2006-46.txt. Layer 1: the law, objectively. Tag conventions are those of coa7-ch1.l4.
-- The clear day rule of s 360(2) comes from coa7-ch7. Seams taken as inputs: `s 971(1)` and `s 969` (coa21).

§§ `Notice of meetings`

-- ---- s 307 Notice required of general meeting --------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:3944 | (A1) This section applies to—
-- src:3945 | (a) a general meeting of a company that is not a traded company; and
-- src:3946 | (b) a general meeting of a traded company that is an opted-in company (as defined by section 971(1)), where—
-- src:3947 | (i) the meeting is held to decide whether to take any action that might result in the frustration of a takeover bid for the company; or
-- src:3948 | (ii) the meeting is held by virtue of section 969 (power of offeror to require general meeting to be held).
@ref s 307(A1) Notice required of general meeting: the meetings this section applies to (src:3944-3948)
GIVEN `the company is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 971(1) the company is an opted-in company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is held to decide whether to take any action that might result in the frustration of a takeover bid for the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 969 the meeting is held by virtue of section 969 (power of offeror to require general meeting to be held)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 307(A1) this section applies to the general meeting` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a traded company`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 971(1) the company is an opted-in company`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the traded company is an opted-in company (s 971(1)) is not known
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies to— (a) ... (b) a general meeting of a traded company that is an opted-in company" does not say "only"
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
             IF `the meeting is held to decide whether to take any action that might result in the frustration of a takeover bid for the company`
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE CONSIDER `s 969 the meeting is held by virtue of section 969 (power of offeror to require general meeting to be held)`
                  WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
                  OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(i) the meeting is held to decide whether to take any action that might result in the frustration of a takeover bid for the company; or (ii) the meeting is held by virtue of section 969"

-- src:3949 | (A2) For corresponding provision(s) in relation to general meetings of traded companies (other than meetings within subsection (A1)(b)), see section 307A.
@ref s 307(A2) Notice required of general meeting: the corresponding provision for traded companies (src:3949)
GIVEN `the company is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is within subsection (A1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 307(A2) section 307A is the corresponding provision for the meeting` MEANS
    IF `the company is a traded company` AND (NOT `the meeting is within subsection (A1)(b)`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to general meetings of traded companies (other than meetings within subsection (A1)(b))" -- FORK F19

-- src:3950 | (1) A general meeting of a private company (other than an adjourned meeting) must be called by notice of at least 14 days.
@ref s 307(1) Notice required of general meeting: private company (src:3950)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is an adjourned meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 307(1) the days of notice required of a general meeting of a private company` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public company` OR `the meeting is an adjourned meeting`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A general meeting of a private company (other than an adjourned meeting)" -- FORK F19
    ELSE JUST 14

-- src:3951 | (2) A general meeting of a public company (other than an adjourned meeting) must be called by notice of—
-- src:3952 | (a) in the case of an annual general meeting, at least 21 days, and
-- src:3953 | (b) in any other case, at least 14 days.
@ref s 307(2) Notice required of general meeting: public company (src:3951-3953)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is an adjourned meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is an annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 307(2) the days of notice required of a general meeting of a public company` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a public company`) OR `the meeting is an adjourned meeting`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A general meeting of a public company (other than an adjourned meeting)" -- FORK F19
    ELSE IF `the meeting is an annual general meeting`
         THEN JUST 21
         ELSE JUST 14

-- src:3954 | (3) The company's articles may require a longer period of notice than that specified in subsection (1) or (2).
@ref s 307(3) Notice required of general meeting: a longer period required by the articles (src:3954)
GIVEN `the days of notice required by subsection (1) or (2)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the days of notice the company's articles require` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 307(3) the days of notice required` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the days of notice required by subsection (1) or (2)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the period under subsection (1) or (2) is not known
    WHEN JUST statutory THEN
        CONSIDER `the days of notice the company's articles require`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST statutory
        WHEN JUST required THEN
            IF required GREATER THAN statutory
            THEN JUST required
            ELSE JUST statutory

-- The notice period is counted in clear days (s 360(1) lists s 307(1) and (2); s 307(3) is taken with them: fork F12).
@ref s 307(3) Notice required of general meeting: the notice given (src:3954)
GIVEN `the days of notice required` IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which notice of the meeting is given` IS A DATE
      `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 307(3) the notice given is at least the notice required` MEANS
    IF `s 360(2) the clear days between the day the notice is given and the day of the meeting` `the day on which notice of the meeting is given` `the day of the meeting` AT LEAST `the days of notice required`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be called by notice of at least 14 days" -- FORK F12

-- src:3955 | (4) A general meeting may be called by shorter notice than that otherwise required if shorter notice is agreed by the members.
@ref s 307(4) Notice required of general meeting: shorter notice (src:3955)
GIVEN `shorter notice is agreed by the members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 307(4) the meeting may be called by shorter notice than otherwise required` MEANS
    IF `shorter notice is agreed by the members`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A general meeting may be called by shorter notice than that otherwise required if shorter notice is agreed by the members" -- FORK F22 -- MARGINAL b

-- A majority in number of the members with a right to attend and vote, who together hold not less than the requisite
-- percentage in nominal value of the shares giving that right (excluding treasury shares); or, with no share capital,
-- together represent not less than the requisite percentage of the total voting rights.
-- src:3956 | (5) The shorter notice must be agreed to by a majority in number of the members having a right to attend and vote at the meeting, being a majority who—
-- src:3957 | (a) together hold not less than the requisite percentage in nominal value of the shares giving a right to attend and vote at the meeting (excluding any shares in the company held as treasury shares), or
-- src:3958 | (b) in the case of a company not having a share capital, together represent not less than the requisite percentage of the total voting rights at that meeting of all the members.
@ref s 307(5) Notice required of general meeting: who must agree to shorter notice (src:3956-3958)
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `members having a right to attend and vote at the meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `of those members, the number who agree to the shorter notice` IS A NUMBER
      `nominal value of the shares held by the agreeing members` IS A NUMBER
      `nominal value of all the shares giving a right to attend and vote at the meeting (excluding treasury shares)` IS A NUMBER
      `voting rights represented by the agreeing members` IS A NUMBER
      `total voting rights at the meeting of all the members` IS A NUMBER
      `the requisite percentage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 307(5) the shorter notice has been agreed to as this subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `of those members, the number who agree to the shorter notice` TIMES 2 GREATER THAN `members having a right to attend and vote at the meeting`
        AND (IF `the company has a share capital`
             THEN `nominal value of the shares held by the agreeing members` AT LEAST `the requisite percentage` TIMES `nominal value of all the shares giving a right to attend and vote at the meeting (excluding treasury shares)`
             ELSE `voting rights represented by the agreeing members` AT LEAST `the requisite percentage` TIMES `total voting rights at the meeting of all the members`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The shorter notice must be agreed to by a majority in number of the members having a right to attend and vote at the meeting, being a majority who— (a) together hold not less than the requisite percentage" -- FORK F5

-- The requisite percentage as a fraction (0.9 is 90%): 90% or a higher percentage in the articles (not exceeding 95%) for a
-- private company; 95% for a public company.
-- src:3959 | (6) The requisite percentage is—
-- src:3960 | (a) in the case of a private company, 90% or such higher percentage (not exceeding 95%) as may be specified in the company's articles;
-- src:3961 | (b) in the case of a public company, 95%.
@ref s 307(6) Notice required of general meeting: the requisite percentage (src:3959-3961)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `higher percentage specified in the company's articles` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 307(6) the requisite percentage` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public company`
    THEN JUST 0.95
    ELSE CONSIDER `higher percentage specified in the company's articles`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST 0.9
         WHEN JUST p THEN
             IF p AT LEAST 0.9 AND p AT MOST 0.95
             THEN JUST p
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "90% or such higher percentage (not exceeding 95%) as may be specified in the company's articles"

-- src:3962 | (7) Subsections (5) and (6) do not apply to an annual general meeting of a public company (see instead section 337(2)).
@ref s 307(7) Notice required of general meeting: annual general meeting of a public company (src:3962)
GIVEN `the meeting is an annual general meeting of a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 307(7) subsections (5) and (6) do not apply to the meeting` MEANS
    IF `the meeting is an annual general meeting of a public company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subsections (5) and (6) do not apply to an annual general meeting of a public company (see instead section 337(2))"

-- ---- s 307A Notice required of general meeting: certain meetings of traded companies ------------------------

-- src:3967 | (2) Condition A is that the general meeting is not an annual general meeting.
@ref s 307A(2) Notice required of general meeting: certain meetings of traded companies: condition A (src:3967)
GIVEN `the general meeting is an annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 307A(2) condition A is met` MEANS
    IF `the general meeting is an annual general meeting`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Condition A is that the general meeting is not an annual general meeting"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:3968 | (3) Condition B is that the company offers the facility for members to vote by electronic means accessible to all members who hold shares that carry rights to vote at general meetings. This condition is met if there is a facility, offered by the company and accessible to all such members, to appoint a proxy by means of a website.
@ref s 307A(3) Notice required of general meeting: certain meetings of traded companies: condition B (src:3968)
GIVEN `the company offers the facility for members to vote by electronic means accessible to all members who hold shares that carry rights to vote at general meetings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a facility, offered by the company and accessible to all such members, to appoint a proxy by means of a website` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 307A(3) condition B is met` MEANS
    IF `the company offers the facility for members to vote by electronic means accessible to all members who hold shares that carry rights to vote at general meetings`
        OR `there is a facility, offered by the company and accessible to all such members, to appoint a proxy by means of a website`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Condition B is that the company offers the facility for members to vote by electronic means accessible to all members who hold shares that carry rights to vote at general meetings"

-- src:3969 | (4) Condition C is that a special resolution reducing the period of notice to not less than 14 days has been passed—
-- src:3970 | (a) at the immediately preceding annual general meeting, or
-- src:3971 | (b) at a general meeting held since that annual general meeting.
@ref s 307A(4) Notice required of general meeting: certain meetings of traded companies: condition C (src:3969-3971)
GIVEN `a special resolution reducing the period of notice to not less than 14 days was passed at the immediately preceding annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a special resolution reducing the period of notice to not less than 14 days was passed at a general meeting held since that annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 307A(4) condition C is met` MEANS
    IF `a special resolution reducing the period of notice to not less than 14 days was passed at the immediately preceding annual general meeting`
        OR `a special resolution reducing the period of notice to not less than 14 days was passed at a general meeting held since that annual general meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Condition C is that a special resolution reducing the period of notice to not less than 14 days has been passed"

-- src:3972 | (5) In the case of a company which has not yet held an annual general meeting, condition C is that a special resolution reducing the period of notice to not less than 14 days has been passed at a general meeting.
@ref s 307A(5) Notice required of general meeting: certain meetings of traded companies: no annual general meeting yet (src:3972)
GIVEN `the company has not yet held an annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a special resolution reducing the period of notice to not less than 14 days has been passed at a general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 307A(5) condition C is met by a company that has not yet held an annual general meeting` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company has not yet held an annual general meeting`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In the case of a company which has not yet held an annual general meeting" -- MARGINAL a
    ELSE IF `a special resolution reducing the period of notice to not less than 14 days has been passed at a general meeting`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "condition C is that a special resolution reducing the period of notice to not less than 14 days has been passed at a general meeting"

-- src:3964 | (1) A general meeting of a traded company must be called by notice of—
-- src:3965 | (a) in a case where conditions A to C (set out below) are met, at least 14 days;
-- src:3966 | (b) in any other case, at least 21 days.
@ref s 307A(1) Notice required of general meeting: certain meetings of traded companies (src:3964-3966)
GIVEN `the meeting is an adjourned meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 307A(2) condition A is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 307A(3) condition B is met` IS A BOOLEAN
      `condition C is met (s 307A(4), or s 307A(5) for a company that has not yet held an annual general meeting)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 307A(1) the days of notice required of a general meeting of a traded company` MEANS
    IF `the meeting is an adjourned meeting`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (7) deals with an adjourned meeting
    ELSE IF `s 307A(2) condition A is met` AND `s 307A(3) condition B is met` AND `condition C is met (s 307A(4), or s 307A(5) for a company that has not yet held an annual general meeting)`
         THEN JUST 14
         ELSE JUST 21

-- src:3973 | (6) The company's articles may require a longer period of notice than that specified in subsection (1).
@ref s 307A(6) Notice required of general meeting: certain meetings of traded companies: a longer period in the articles (src:3973)
GIVEN `the days of notice required by subsection (1)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the days of notice the company's articles require` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 307A(6) the days of notice required` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the days of notice required by subsection (1)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the period under subsection (1) is not known
    WHEN JUST statutory THEN
        CONSIDER `the days of notice the company's articles require`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST statutory
        WHEN JUST required THEN
            IF required GREATER THAN statutory
            THEN JUST required
            ELSE JUST statutory

-- An adjourned meeting may be called by shorter notice; but after an adjournment for lack of a quorum only if no business
-- is to be dealt with of a general nature not stated in the notice of the original meeting, and the adjourned meeting is
-- held at least 10 days after the original meeting.
-- src:3974 | (7) Where a general meeting is adjourned, the adjourned meeting may be called by shorter notice than required by subsection (1). But in the case of an adjournment for lack of a quorum this subsection applies only if—
-- src:3975 | (a) no business is to be dealt with at the adjourned meeting the general nature of which was not stated in the notice of the original meeting, and
-- src:3976 | (b) the adjourned meeting is to be held at least 10 days after the original meeting.
@ref s 307A(7) Notice required of general meeting: certain meetings of traded companies: adjourned meetings (src:3974-3976)
GIVEN `the meeting is an adjourned meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting was adjourned for lack of a quorum` IS A BOOLEAN
      `no business is to be dealt with at the adjourned meeting the general nature of which was not stated in the notice of the original meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the original meeting` IS A DATE
      `the date of the adjourned meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 307A(7) the adjourned meeting may be called by shorter notice` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the meeting is an adjourned meeting`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a general meeting is adjourned" -- MARGINAL a
    ELSE IF (NOT `the meeting was adjourned for lack of a quorum`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE IF `no business is to be dealt with at the adjourned meeting the general nature of which was not stated in the notice of the original meeting`
                 AND `the date of the adjourned meeting` AT LEAST `the date of the original meeting` PLUS 10
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of an adjournment for lack of a quorum this subsection applies only if— (a) ... and (b) the adjourned meeting is to be held at least 10 days after the original meeting"

-- src:3977 | (8) Nothing in this section applies in relation to a general meeting of a kind mentioned in section 307(A1)(b) (certain meetings regarding takeover of opted-in company).
@ref s 307A(8) Notice required of general meeting: certain meetings of traded companies: opted-in takeover meetings (src:3977)
GIVEN `the meeting is of a kind mentioned in section 307(A1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 307A(8) nothing in this section applies to the meeting` MEANS
    IF `the meeting is of a kind mentioned in section 307(A1)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Nothing in this section applies in relation to a general meeting of a kind mentioned in section 307(A1)(b)"

-- ---- s 308 Manner in which notice to be given --------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 308 manner of giving notice` IS ONE OF
    `s 308(a) in hard copy form`
    `s 308(b) in electronic form`
    `s 308(c) by means of a website (see section 309)`
    `s 308 partly by one such means and partly by another`
    `s 308 some other manner`

-- src:3979 | Notice of a general meeting of a company must be given—
-- src:3980 | (a) in hard copy form,
-- src:3981 | (b) in electronic form, or
-- src:3982 | (c) by means of a website (see section 309),
-- src:3983 | or partly by one such means and partly by another.
@ref s 308 Manner in which notice to be given (src:3979-3983)
GIVEN manner IS A `s 308 manner of giving notice`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 308 the notice of the general meeting is given in a manner this section allows` MEANS
    CONSIDER manner
    WHEN `s 308 some other manner` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Notice of a general meeting of a company must be given— (a) in hard copy form, (b) in electronic form, or (c) by means of a website" -- FORK F5
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 309 Publication of notice of meeting on website -----------------------------------------------------

-- src:3986 | (2) When the company notifies a member of the presence of the notice on the website the notification must—
-- src:3987 | (a) state that it concerns a notice of a company meeting,
-- src:3988 | (b) specify the place, date and time of the meeting, and
-- src:3989 | (c) in the case of a public company, state whether the meeting will be an annual general meeting.
@ref s 309(2) Publication of notice of meeting on website: the notification (src:3986-3989)
GIVEN `the notification states that it concerns a notice of a company meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notification specifies the place, date and time of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notification states whether the meeting will be an annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 309(2) the notification to the member meets the requirements of this subsection` MEANS
    IF `the notification states that it concerns a notice of a company meeting`
        AND `the notification specifies the place, date and time of the meeting`
        AND ((NOT `the company is a public company`) OR `the notification states whether the meeting will be an annual general meeting`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the notification must— (a) state that it concerns a notice of a company meeting, (b) specify the place, date and time of the meeting, and (c) in the case of a public company, state whether the meeting will be an annual general meeting" -- FORK F5

-- src:3990 | (3) The notice must be available on the website throughout the period beginning with the date of that notification and ending with the conclusion of the meeting.
@ref s 309(3) Publication of notice of meeting on website: availability (src:3990)
GIVEN `the date of the notification` IS A DATE
      `the first day on which the notice was available on the website` IS A DATE
      `the last day on which the notice was available on the website` IS A DATE
      `the day of the conclusion of the meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 309(3) the notice was available on the website throughout the period this subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the first day on which the notice was available on the website` AT MOST `the date of the notification`
        AND `the last day on which the notice was available on the website` AT LEAST `the day of the conclusion of the meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must be available on the website throughout the period beginning with the date of that notification and ending with the conclusion of the meeting" -- FORK F5

-- TRUE says the bar holds (the notice is not validly given); FALSE says the bar does not apply (ruling of 2026-11-05 (d)).
-- src:3985 | (1) Notice of a meeting is not validly given by a company by means of a website unless it is given in accordance with this section.
@ref s 309(1) Publication of notice of meeting on website: validity (src:3985)
GIVEN `the notice is given in accordance with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 309(1) notice given by means of a website is not validly given` MEANS
    IF `the notice is given in accordance with this section`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Notice of a meeting is not validly given by a company by means of a website unless it is given in accordance with this section" -- FORK F8
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 310 Persons entitled to receive notice of meetings --------------------------------------------------

-- src:3992 | (1) Notice of a general meeting of a company must be sent to—
-- src:3993 | (a) every member of the company, and
-- src:3994 | (b) every director.
@ref s 310(1) Persons entitled to receive notice of meetings (src:3992-3994)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 310(1) notice of a general meeting must be sent to the person` MEANS
    IF `the person is a member of the company` OR `the person is a director`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "must be sent to— (a) every member of the company, and (b) every director"

-- src:3995 | (2) In subsection (1), the reference to members includes any person who is entitled to a share in consequence of the death or bankruptcy of a member, if the company has been notified of their entitlement.
@ref s 310(2) Persons entitled to receive notice of meetings: death or bankruptcy of a member (src:3995)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to a share in consequence of the death or bankruptcy of a member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has been notified of their entitlement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 310(2) the person is a member for the purposes of subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the person is entitled to a share in consequence of the death or bankruptcy of a member`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the reference to members includes any person who is entitled to a share in consequence of the death or bankruptcy of a member"
    ELSE IF `the company has been notified of their entitlement`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the company has been notified of their entitlement" -- MARGINAL a

DECLARE `s 310(3) event` IS ONE OF
    `s 310(3)(a) the sequestration of the estate of a member`
    `s 310(3)(b) a member's estate being the subject of a protected trust deed (within the meaning of the Bankruptcy (Scotland) Act 2016)`
    `s 310(3) another event`

-- src:3996 | (3) In subsection (2), the reference to the bankruptcy of a member includes—
-- src:3997 | (a) the sequestration of the estate of a member;
-- src:3998 | (b) a member's estate being the subject of a protected trust deed (within the meaning of the Bankruptcy (Scotland) Act 2016).
@ref s 310(3) Persons entitled to receive notice of meetings: bankruptcy (src:3996-3998)
GIVEN event IS A `s 310(3) event`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 310(3) the event is within the reference to the bankruptcy of a member` MEANS
    CONSIDER event
    WHEN `s 310(3) another event` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the reference to the bankruptcy of a member includes"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:3999 | (4) This section has effect subject to—
-- src:4000 | (a) any enactment, and
-- src:4001 | (b) any provision of the company's articles.
@ref s 310(4) Persons entitled to receive notice of meetings: subject to enactments and the articles (src:3999-4001)
GIVEN `an enactment provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's articles provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 310(4) the rule of this section has effect` MEANS
    IF `an enactment provides otherwise` OR `the company's articles provide otherwise`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section has effect subject to— (a) any enactment, and (b) any provision of the company's articles" -- FORK F4 -- MARGINAL b
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 311 Contents of notices of meetings -----------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4003 | (1) Notice of a general meeting of a company must state—
-- src:4004 | (a) the time and date of the meeting, and
-- src:4005 | (b) the place of the meeting.
@ref s 311(1) Contents of notices of meetings: time, date and place (src:4003-4005)
GIVEN `the notice states the time and date of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the place of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 311(1) the notice states what this subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the notice states the time and date of the meeting` AND `the notice states the place of the meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Notice of a general meeting of a company must state— (a) the time and date of the meeting, and (b) the place of the meeting" -- FORK F5

-- src:4006 | (2) Notice of a general meeting of a company must state the general nature of the business to be dealt with at the meeting.
-- src:4007 | In relation to a company other than a traded company, this subsection has effect subject to any provision of the company's articles.
@ref s 311(2) Contents of notices of meetings: the business (src:4006-4007)
GIVEN `the company is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the general nature of the business to be dealt with at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's articles provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 311(2) the notice states what this subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the notice states the general nature of the business to be dealt with at the meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF (NOT `the company is a traded company`) AND `the company's articles provide otherwise`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "In relation to a company other than a traded company, this subsection has effect subject to any provision of the company's articles" -- FORK F19
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Notice of a general meeting of a company must state the general nature of the business to be dealt with at the meeting" -- FORK F5

-- src:4008 | (3) Notice of a general meeting of a traded company must also include—
-- src:4009 | (a) a statement giving the address of the website on which the information required by section 311A (traded companies: publication of information in advance of general meeting) is published;
-- src:4010 | (b) a statement—
-- src:4011 | (i) that the right to vote at the meeting is determined by reference to the register of members ..., and
-- src:4012 | (ii) of the time when that right will be determined in accordance with section 360B(2) (traded companies: share dealings before general meetings);
-- src:4013 | (c) a statement of the procedures with which members must comply in order to be able to attend and vote at the meeting (including the date by which they must comply);
-- src:4014 | (d) a statement giving details of any forms to be used for the appointment of a proxy;
-- src:4015 | (e) where the company offers the facility for members to vote in advance (see section 322A) or by electronic means (see section 360A), a statement of the procedure for doing so (including the date by which it must be done, and details of any forms to be used); and
-- src:4016 | (f) a statement of the right of members to ask questions in accordance with section 319A (traded companies: questions at meetings).
@ref s 311(3) Contents of notices of meetings: traded companies (src:4008-4016)
GIVEN `the company is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice gives the address of the website on which the information required by section 311A is published` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states that the right to vote at the meeting is determined by reference to the register of members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the time when that right will be determined in accordance with section 360B(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the procedures with which members must comply in order to be able to attend and vote at the meeting (including the date by which they must comply)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice gives details of any forms to be used for the appointment of a proxy` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company offers the facility for members to vote in advance (see section 322A) or by electronic means (see section 360A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the procedure for voting in advance or by electronic means (including the date by which it must be done, and details of any forms to be used)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the right of members to ask questions in accordance with section 319A` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 311(3) the notice of the traded company includes the statements this subsection requires` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a traded company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Notice of a general meeting of a traded company must also include"
    ELSE IF `the notice gives the address of the website on which the information required by section 311A is published`
            AND `the notice states that the right to vote at the meeting is determined by reference to the register of members`
            AND `the notice states the time when that right will be determined in accordance with section 360B(2)`
            AND `the notice states the procedures with which members must comply in order to be able to attend and vote at the meeting (including the date by which they must comply)`
            AND `the notice gives details of any forms to be used for the appointment of a proxy`
            AND ((NOT `the company offers the facility for members to vote in advance (see section 322A) or by electronic means (see section 360A)`)
                 OR `the notice states the procedure for voting in advance or by electronic means (including the date by which it must be done, and details of any forms to be used)`)
            AND `the notice states the right of members to ask questions in accordance with section 319A`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Notice of a general meeting of a traded company must also include— (a) ... (f) a statement of the right of members to ask questions" -- FORK F5

-- ---- s 311A Traded companies: publication of information in advance of general meeting ---------------------

-- src:4018 | (1) A traded company must ensure that the following information relating to a general meeting of the company is made available on a website—
-- src:4019 | (a) the matters set out in the notice of the meeting;
-- src:4020 | (b) the total numbers of—
-- src:4021 | (i) shares in the company, and
-- src:4022 | (ii) shares of each class,
-- src:4023 | in respect of which members are entitled to exercise voting rights at the meeting;
-- src:4024 | (c) the totals of the voting rights that members are entitled to exercise at the meeting in respect of the shares of each class;
-- src:4025 | (d) members' statements, members' resolutions and members' matters of business received by the company after the first date on which notice of the meeting is given.
@ref s 311A(1) Traded companies: publication of information in advance of general meeting (src:4018-4025)
GIVEN `the company is a traded company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the matters set out in the notice of the meeting are made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total numbers of shares, and of shares of each class, in respect of which members are entitled to exercise voting rights at the meeting are made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the totals of the voting rights that members are entitled to exercise at the meeting in respect of the shares of each class are made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `members' statements, members' resolutions and members' matters of business received after the first date on which notice of the meeting is given are made available on a website` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 311A(1) the traded company has made the information available on a website` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the company is a traded company`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A traded company must ensure"
    ELSE IF `the matters set out in the notice of the meeting are made available on a website`
            AND `the total numbers of shares, and of shares of each class, in respect of which members are entitled to exercise voting rights at the meeting are made available on a website`
            AND `the totals of the voting rights that members are entitled to exercise at the meeting in respect of the shares of each class are made available on a website`
            AND `members' statements, members' resolutions and members' matters of business received after the first date on which notice of the meeting is given are made available on a website`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A traded company must ensure that the following information relating to a general meeting of the company is made available on a website" -- FORK F5

-- src:4026 | (2) The information must be made available on a website that—
-- src:4027 | (a) is maintained by or on behalf of the company, and
-- src:4028 | (b) identifies the company.
@ref s 311A(2) Traded companies: publication of information in advance of general meeting: the website (src:4026-4028)
GIVEN `the website is maintained by or on behalf of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the website identifies the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 311A(2) the website is one this subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the website is maintained by or on behalf of the company` AND `the website identifies the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The information must be made available on a website that— (a) is maintained by or on behalf of the company, and (b) identifies the company" -- FORK F5

-- src:4029 | (3) Access to the information on the website, and the ability to obtain a hard copy of the information from the website, must not be conditional on payment of a fee or otherwise restricted.
@ref s 311A(3) Traded companies: publication of information in advance of general meeting: no fee (src:4029)
GIVEN `access to the information, or the ability to obtain a hard copy of it from the website, is conditional on payment of a fee or otherwise restricted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 311A(3) access to the information is as this subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `access to the information, or the ability to obtain a hard copy of it from the website, is conditional on payment of a fee or otherwise restricted`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Access to the information on the website, and the ability to obtain a hard copy of the information from the website, must not be conditional on payment of a fee or otherwise restricted"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4032 | (i) in the case of information required by subsection (1)(a) to (c), on or before the first date on which notice of the meeting is given, and
@ref s 311A(4)(a)(i) Traded companies: publication of information in advance of general meeting: time for (1)(a) to (c) (src:4032)
GIVEN `the date on which the information required by subsection (1)(a) to (c) was made available` IS A DATE
      `the first date on which notice of the meeting is given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 311A(4)(a)(i) the information required by subsection (1)(a) to (c) was made available in time` MEANS
    IF `the date on which the information required by subsection (1)(a) to (c) was made available` AT MOST `the first date on which notice of the meeting is given`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on or before the first date on which notice of the meeting is given"

-- src:4033 | (ii) in the case of information required by subsection (1)(d), as soon as reasonably practicable, and
@ref s 311A(4)(a)(ii) Traded companies: publication of information in advance of general meeting: time for (1)(d) (src:4033)
GIVEN `the information required by subsection (1)(d) was made available as soon as reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 311A(4)(a)(ii) the information required by subsection (1)(d) was made available in time` MEANS
    IF `the information required by subsection (1)(d) was made available as soon as reasonably practicable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of information required by subsection (1)(d), as soon as reasonably practicable"

-- "throughout the period of two years beginning with the date on which it is first made available": the last day of
-- that period is the day before the second anniversary of that date.
-- src:4034 | (b) must be kept available throughout the period of two years beginning with the date on which it is first made available on a website in accordance with this section.
@ref s 311A(4)(b) Traded companies: publication of information in advance of general meeting: kept available for two years (src:4034)
GIVEN `the date on which the information was first made available on a website` IS A DATE
      `the last day on which the information was kept available` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 311A(4)(b) the information was kept available throughout the two years` MEANS
    IF `the last day on which the information was kept available` AT LEAST (`add years` `the date on which the information was first made available on a website` 2) MINUS 1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be kept available throughout the period of two years beginning with the date on which it is first made available" -- FORK F7

-- src:4035 | (5) A failure to make information available throughout the period specified in subsection (4)(b) is disregarded if—
-- src:4036 | (a) the information is made available on the website for part of that period, and
-- src:4037 | (b) the failure is wholly attributable to circumstances that it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid.
@ref s 311A(5) Traded companies: publication of information in advance of general meeting: a failure disregarded (src:4035-4037)
GIVEN `the information is made available on the website for part of the period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure is wholly attributable to circumstances that it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 311A(5) the failure to make the information available throughout the period is disregarded` MEANS
    IF `the information is made available on the website for part of the period`
        AND `the failure is wholly attributable to circumstances that it would not be reasonable to have expected the company to prevent or avoid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A failure to make information available throughout the period specified in subsection (4)(b) is disregarded if" -- MARGINAL a

-- src:4038 | (6) The amounts mentioned in subsection (1)(b) and (c) must be ascertained at the latest practicable time before the first date on which notice of the meeting is given.
@ref s 311A(6) Traded companies: publication of information in advance of general meeting: the amounts (src:4038)
GIVEN `the amounts were ascertained at the latest practicable time before the first date on which notice of the meeting is given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 311A(6) the amounts mentioned in subsection (1)(b) and (c) were ascertained as this subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the amounts were ascertained at the latest practicable time before the first date on which notice of the meeting is given`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The amounts mentioned in subsection (1)(b) and (c) must be ascertained at the latest practicable time before the first date on which notice of the meeting is given" -- FORK F5

-- src:4039 | (7) Failure to comply with this section does not affect the validity of the meeting or of anything done at the meeting.
@ref s 311A(7) Traded companies: publication of information in advance of general meeting: validity (src:4039)
GIVEN `the company failed to comply with this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 311A(7) the failure affects the validity of the meeting or of anything done at the meeting` MEANS
    IF `the company failed to comply with this section`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Failure to comply with this section does not affect the validity of the meeting or of anything done at the meeting."
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of a failure to comply
-- src:4040 | (8) If this section is not complied with as respects any meeting, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 311A(8) Traded companies: publication of information in advance of general meeting: offence (src:4040)
GIVEN `this section is not complied with as respects the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 311A(8) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF `this section is not complied with as respects the meeting`
    THEN `s 1121 the officer is in default`
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If this section is not complied with as respects any meeting, an offence is committed by every officer of the company who is in default." -- MARGINAL a
-- src:4041 | (9) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 311A(9) Traded companies: publication of information in advance of general meeting: penalty (src:4041)
GIVEN `how the person is convicted` IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 311A(9) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `how the person is convicted`
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is liable on summary conviction"
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, NOTHING, JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1), NOTHING, FALSE)

-- ---- s 312 Resolution requiring special notice -------------------------------------------------------------

-- The bar: TRUE says the resolution is not effective; FALSE says the bar does not apply (it is not said to be effective).
-- src:4043 | (1) Where by any provision of the Companies Acts special notice is required of a resolution, the resolution is not effective unless notice of the intention to move it has been given to the company at least 28 days before the meeting at which it is moved.
@ref s 312(1) Resolution requiring special notice (src:4043)
GIVEN `the day on which notice of the intention to move the resolution was given to the company` IS A DATE
      `the day of the meeting at which the resolution is moved` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 312(1) the resolution is not effective` MEANS
    IF `s 360(2) the clear days between the day the notice is given and the day of the meeting` `the day on which notice of the intention to move the resolution was given to the company` `the day of the meeting at which the resolution is moved` AT LEAST 28
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the resolution is not effective unless notice of the intention to move it has been given to the company at least 28 days before the meeting at which it is moved" -- FORK F8
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:4044 | (2) The company must, where practicable, give its members notice of any such resolution in the same manner and at the same time as it gives notice of the meeting.
@ref s 312(2) Resolution requiring special notice: notice to the members (src:4044)
GIVEN `it is practicable to give the members notice of the resolution in the same manner and at the same time as notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company gives its members notice of the resolution in the same manner and at the same time as it gives notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 312(2) the company has given its members notice of the resolution as this subsection requires` MEANS
    IF (NOT `it is practicable to give the members notice of the resolution in the same manner and at the same time as notice of the meeting`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The company must, where practicable, give its members notice of any such resolution in the same manner and at the same time as it gives notice of the meeting"
    ELSE IF `the company gives its members notice of the resolution in the same manner and at the same time as it gives notice of the meeting`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company must, where practicable, give its members notice" -- FORK F5

DECLARE `s 312(3) manner of giving notice` IS ONE OF
    `s 312(3)(a) by advertisement in a newspaper having an appropriate circulation`
    `s 312(3)(b) in any other manner allowed by the company's articles`
    `s 312(3) some other manner`

-- src:4045 | (3) Where that is not practicable, the company must give its members notice at least 14 days before the meeting—
-- src:4046 | (a) by advertisement in a newspaper having an appropriate circulation, or
-- src:4047 | (b) in any other manner allowed by the company's articles.
@ref s 312(3) Resolution requiring special notice: where giving notice with the notice of the meeting is not practicable (src:4045-4047)
GIVEN `it is practicable to give the members notice of the resolution in the same manner and at the same time as notice of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the company gave its members notice of the resolution` IS A DATE
      `the day of the meeting` IS A DATE
      manner IS A `s 312(3) manner of giving notice`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 312(3) the company has given its members notice at least 14 days before the meeting in a manner this subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `it is practicable to give the members notice of the resolution in the same manner and at the same time as notice of the meeting`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where that is not practicable, the company must give its members notice at least 14 days before the meeting"
    ELSE CONSIDER manner
         WHEN `s 312(3) some other manner` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must give its members notice at least 14 days before the meeting— (a) by advertisement in a newspaper having an appropriate circulation, or (b) in any other manner allowed by the company's articles" -- FORK F5
         OTHERWISE
             IF `s 360(2) the clear days between the day the notice is given and the day of the meeting` `the day on which the company gave its members notice of the resolution` `the day of the meeting` AT LEAST 14
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the company must give its members notice at least 14 days before the meeting" -- FORK F5

-- (4) "a meeting is called for a date 28 days or less after the notice has been given": the plain difference of the two days
-- (the clear day rule of s 360 is not listed for this subsection).
-- src:4048 | (4) If, after notice of the intention to move such a resolution has been given to the company, a meeting is called for a date 28 days or less after the notice has been given, the notice is deemed to have been properly given, though not given within the time required.
@ref s 312(4) Resolution requiring special notice: a meeting called at short notice (src:4048)
GIVEN `the day on which notice of the intention to move the resolution was given to the company` IS A DATE
      `the date for which the meeting is called` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 312(4) the notice is deemed to have been properly given though not given within the time required` MEANS
    IF `the date for which the meeting is called` AT MOST `the day on which notice of the intention to move the resolution was given to the company` PLUS 28
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, after notice of the intention to move such a resolution has been given to the company, a meeting is called for a date 28 days or less after the notice has been given" -- MARGINAL a

-- ---- s 313 Accidental failure to give notice of resolution or meeting ----------------------------------------

-- src:4050 | (1) Where a company gives notice of—
-- src:4051 | (a) a general meeting, or
-- src:4052 | (b) a resolution intended to be moved at a general meeting,
-- src:4053 | any accidental failure to give notice to one or more persons shall be disregarded for the purpose of determining whether notice of the meeting or resolution (as the case may be) is duly given.
@ref s 313(1) Accidental failure to give notice of resolution or meeting (src:4050-4053)
GIVEN `the company gives notice of a general meeting or of a resolution intended to be moved at a general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure to give notice to one or more persons was accidental` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 313(1) the failure is disregarded in determining whether notice is duly given` MEANS
    IF `the company gives notice of a general meeting or of a resolution intended to be moved at a general meeting` AND `the failure to give notice to one or more persons was accidental`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any accidental failure to give notice to one or more persons shall be disregarded"

DECLARE `s 313(2) notice` IS ONE OF
    `s 313(2)(a) notice given under section 304 (notice of meetings required by members)`
    `s 313(2)(b) notice given under section 305 (notice of meetings called by members)`
    `s 313(2)(c) notice given under section 339 (notice of resolutions at AGMs proposed by members)`
    `s 313(2) any other notice`

-- src:4054 | (2) Except in relation to notice given under—
-- src:4055 | (a) section 304 (notice of meetings required by members),
-- src:4056 | (b) section 305 (notice of meetings called by members), or
-- src:4057 | (c) section 339 (notice of resolutions at AGMs proposed by members),
-- src:4058 | subsection (1) has effect subject to any provision of the company's articles.
@ref s 313(2) Accidental failure to give notice of resolution or meeting: subject to the articles (src:4054-4058)
GIVEN notice IS A `s 313(2) notice`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 313(2) subsection (1) has effect subject to any provision of the company's articles` MEANS
    CONSIDER notice
    WHEN `s 313(2) any other notice` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except in relation to notice given under— (a) section 304 ..., (b) section 305 ..., or (c) section 339 ..., subsection (1) has effect subject to any provision of the company's articles" -- FORK F19
